WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.000
Find seven days with sunlight and Earth in view.
Southlight connects NASA geometry and lunar terrain.

00:03.000 --> 00:08.000
Connecting Ridge, 1 January 2027: sunlight 100%,
but Earth is hidden for the entire seven-day window.

00:08.000 --> 00:13.500
Select an unavailable period. The shared cursor
reveals the terrain obstruction in the skyline.

00:13.500 --> 00:19.000
Find a better window. The scene accelerates
through real dates, then slows at the recommendation.

00:19.000 --> 00:24.000
Start nine days later: both are visible for 100%
of the sampled window. The original stays beside it.

00:24.000 --> 00:28.200
Inspect NASA sources, direction validation and
terrain sensitivity. Visibility is not landing safety.

00:28.200 --> 00:29.600
Southlight. A clearer view of the next landing.
